# Build output
/bin/
/dist/
*.exe

# The admin UI's build output. internal/adminui/dist/.gitkeep is committed and
# has to stay that way — it is what lets `go build` succeed with no Node
# installed, since go:embed refuses a directory it can find nothing in — but
# everything vite writes beside it is generated and belongs to whoever last ran
# `make ui-build`.
#
# This is load-bearing beyond tidiness. goreleaser refuses to build from a dirty
# tree, and .goreleaser.yaml runs ui-build as a before-hook, so a bundle that
# read as an untracked file would make every release fail on the output of its
# own build step.
/internal/adminui/dist/*
!/internal/adminui/dist/.gitkeep

# The pnpm store for the JavaScript workspace, at the root and in every package.
node_modules/

# Release artifacts the publish job writes into the working directory before
# goreleaser runs: `helm package` drops the chart tarball in the current
# directory, and the SBOM action writes its document beside it. goreleaser
# refuses to build from a dirty tree — rightly, since it cannot tell a stray
# artifact from an uncommitted source edit — and it honours .gitignore, so
# naming them here is what keeps that check meaningful rather than disabling it.
/mockulus-*.tgz
/*.spdx.json

# Test & coverage artifacts
/test/e2e/.artifacts/
/test/load/.results/
*.out
*.test
coverage.txt
covdata/

# Local tooling
/.tools/

# npm toolchain. pnpm-lock.yaml is committed — it is the reproducibility
# guarantee, same role as go.sum.
node_modules/
/ui/dist/

# The browser smoke's own output: traces and screenshots kept from a failing
# run, and the HTML report built over them. Both are evidence about one run on
# one machine, which is a thing to read and then throw away.
/ui/test-results/
/ui/playwright-report/
/ui/blob-report/

# The embedded admin UI bundle. `internal/adminui` embeds this directory with
# `//go:embed all:dist`, so the built site is an input to `go build` rather than
# a leftover of it — but it is still generated, and generated bundles do not
# belong in the tree.
#
# `.gitkeep` is the exception and stays tracked: go:embed fails on a directory
# that does not exist, and that placeholder is what keeps `go build` working on
# a machine with no Node installed. Ignoring the contents rather than the
# directory itself is what leaves room for the negation to apply.
/internal/adminui/dist/*
!/internal/adminui/dist/.gitkeep

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# Stray binaries from `go build ./test/e2e/runner` without -o, which names the
# output after the package directory and drops it in the working directory.
/runner
/mockulus

# Internal working documents: the decision log and the differential findings.
# Deliberation rather than product — half-settled positions and the reasoning
# behind calls that were made and unmade. Anything in them a user needs is in
# SPEC.md or the deviation list.
/internalDocs/

# The TypeScript SDK's compiled output. Published to npm from CI, never from a
# working tree, so the tree carries the source and the tarball carries this.
/sdk/typescript/dist/
/sdk/typescript/*.tsbuildinfo

# The contract lint compiles to the repo root when built rather than run.
/contractlint
